nodecode-headroom is a rewrite of seongj-un's seongj-un/hermes-headroom:

  https://github.com/seongj-un/hermes-headroom
  commit a98a64bfb20595c2e26d88fb0a90f4205f37db31
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seongj-un (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the classifier's command families and its command-word reading, the auto
budgets (reserve, minimum start, critical line, slots), the lighten table and its Node heap
cap, the queue with its timeout and its refusal, the watchdog that stops the newest heavy
job, the status picture as a tool and a slash command, and the words the model is told
after a wait or a kill. Left out: the systemd --user scope (a hard MemoryMax, an OOM score,
cgroup peak and OOM-kill readings) and the flock slot pool shared across processes, because
Nodecode has no seam that hands one child to systemd and runs one image rather than several
profiles; and the selftest, which existed to prove the scope. The Hermes-only surfaces --
the pre-LLM hook returning context, the CLI subcommand, the plugin storage directory -- are
carried as a :ROUND reminder, a slash command, and an in-memory event log.
